      <div type="clause" n="El. 49.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 49.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="42" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Ða apostolas ⁊ þa eldran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.37"/> broðor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.star2"/> hælo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.38"/> eow wyscað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.39"/>; ⁊ we éow cyðað, þæt we geascodon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.40"/>, þæt ure geferan sume mid uru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wordum to eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.41"/> comon ⁊ eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.41"/> hefigran [wisan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.42"/> budon] to healdanne þonne we him<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.43"/> budon, ⁊ eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.41"/> to swiðe gedwealdon mid ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.44"/> mannigfealdum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="45" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.45"/> gebodum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="46" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.46"/>, ⁊ eowra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="47" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.47"/> sawla ma forhwerfdon þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1"/> geryhton.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.2"/> Ða gesomnodon we us ymb ðæt, ⁊ ús eallum gelicode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.3"/> ða, þæt we sendon Paulus ⁊ Barnaban<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.4"/>; ða men wilniað hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.5"/> sawla sellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.6"/> for Dryhtnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.7"/> naman.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.3" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="42" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Ða apostolas ⁊ þa ieldran broðor hælo eow wyrcað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.2-4"/>; ⁊ we eow cyðað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> we geahsodon, ðæt úre geferan sume mid urum wordum tó eow comon ⁊ eow hefigran wisan budan to healdanne ðonne we hym budon, ⁊ eow tó swiðe gedwealdon mid þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> monigfealdu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gebodu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, ⁊ eowra sawla ma forhwyrfdon ðonne hie rihton. Ða gesamnodan wé ús ymb þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>, ⁊ ús ða eallum gelicode, ðæt we sendan Paulus ⁊ Barnaban; ða men willað hyra saula sellan for Drihtnes naman.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="43" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Þa apostolas ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.10"/> þa yldran broþra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.20"/> hælo eow wyscað; ⁊ we eow cyþað, þæt we geaxodon, ðæt ure geferan sume mid urum wordum to eow coman ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.2-2"/> eow hefigran wisan budon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.2-2"/> to healdonne ðonne we him budon, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> eow swyðe gedweldon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.2-2"/> mid ðam monigfealdum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> gebodum, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> eowra sawla má forhwyrfdon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.3-2"/> ðonne heo gerihton. Ða gesomnodon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.4-2"/> we us ymb ðæt, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> us eallum ða gelicode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, þæt we sendon Paulus ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/> Barnaban, ða<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.6-2"/> gewilniað hira sawla (to<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.7-2"/>) syllanne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.8"/> for Dryhtnes noman.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="43" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Apostoli et seniores fratres his <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.star"/>qui sunt Antiochię, Sirię et Cilicię<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.15"/> fratribus ex<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.18"/>gentibus salutem. Quoniam audiuimus, quod quidam ex nobis exeuntes turbauerunt uos uerbis, potius euertentes animas uestras, quibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.1-3"/> non mandauimus, placuit nobis collectis in unum eligere uiros et mittere ad uos cum karissimis nostris Barnaba et Paulo, hominibus qui tradere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.oe.2-3"/> cupiunt animas suas pro nomine domini nostri Iesu Christi.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 49.3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="266" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Ða apostolas ⁊ þa eldran broðor hælo eow wyscað; ⁊ we eów cyðað, þæt we geascodon, þæt ure geferan sume mid uru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wordum to eow comon ⁊ eow hefigran to healdanne þonne we him budon, ⁊ eow to swiðe gedwealdon mid ðam mannigfealdum gebodum, ⁊ eowra sawla ma forhwerfdon þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> hie geryhton. Ða gesomnodon we us ymb ðæt, ⁊ ús eallum gelicode ða, þæt we sendon Paulus ⁊ Barnaban; ða men wilniað hiora sawla sellan for Dryhtnes naman.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="43" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Die Apostel und die älteren Brüder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.2"/> wünschen euch Heil! Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.3"/> wir thun euch kund, dass wir erfahren haben, dass einige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.4"/> von unseren Gefährten mit unseren Worten zu euch gekommen sind und euch schwerere Lebensweise<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.5"/> zu halten geboten haben, denn wir ihnen geboten, und euch zu sehr mit den vielfachen Geboten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.5"/> beirrt haben und eure Seelen mehr verdreht als sie zurecht gewiesen haben. Da versammelten wir uns deshalb, und uns allen schien nun richtig, dass wir Paulus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.6"/> und Barnabas absendeten; diese Männer streben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-3.lnote.de.7"/>, ihre Seelen hinzugeben für den Namen des Herrn.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">‘The apostles and the elder brethren wish you salvation! And we make known to you that we have learned that some of our companions have come to you with our words and have commanded you to keep a harder way of life than we commanded them, and have led you too much astray with the manifold commandments and have perverted your souls more than they have set them right. Then we assembled on that account, and it now seemed right to us all that we should send Paul and Barnabas; these men strive to give up their souls for the name of the Lord.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="267" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>“The apostles and the elder brothers wish you health; and we declare to you that we learned, that some of our fellowship came to you with our words and [imposed] on you a heavier burden than we asked, and too greatly led you astray with manifold ordinances, and have ensnared your souls more than they have righted them. Then we assembled ourselves concerning that, and it pleased all of us, that we should send Paul and Barnabas: those men wish to give their souls for the name of the Lord.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Acts 15,23–26</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="43, 45">A Apost. 15.23; A Apost. 15.24; A Apost. 15.25; A Apost. 15.26</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[A Apost. 15, 23] | [15, 24] | [15, 25] | [15, 26]</note>
